# USSLP compose — copy to deploy/compose/.env and edit.
#
# Only the prod-like profile reads these; the dev profile is deliberately
# credential-free so that `docker compose up` needs no preparation.
#
# Every value here is a *parameter with a default*, not a fact about a real
# deployment. Nothing in this repository knows a real password, endpoint or
# account id, and nothing here should be committed with one.

# Image tag and the version stamped into every binary, every metric's `version`
# label and /healthz. Defaults to "prod-like".
USSLP_VERSION=prod-like

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Infrastructure credentials (prod-like only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
POSTGRES_USER=usslp
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=usslp-change-me

CLICKHOUSE_USER=usslp
CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD=usslp-change-me

GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=usslp-change-me

# EMQX clusters on an Erlang distribution cookie. A single-node compose profile
# does not cluster, but the value is still what an attacker with network access
# would need to join one, so it is a parameter rather than a default in the file.
EMQX_NODE_COOKIE=usslp-prod-like-cookie
EMQX_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=usslp-change-me

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The UIG operator token gates /v1/bindings, /v1/deliveries and /v1/replay.
# prod-like reads it from a compose secret file rather than an environment
# variable, because config.Loader resolves USSLP_UIG_OPERATOR_TOKEN_FILE before
# USSLP_UIG_OPERATOR_TOKEN (platform/pkg/config/config.go). Edit
# deploy/compose/secrets/uig-operator-token, not this file.
